WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:07.340
My name is Wade Watts. My dad picked that name because it sounded like a superhero's alter-ego.

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:10.080
Like Peter Parker or Bruce Banner.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.980
But he died when I was a kid. My mom, too.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:17.420
And I ended up here.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:23.779
Sitting here my tiny corner of nowhere. There's nowhere left to go.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.500
Nowhere...

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.160
Except the Oasis.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:38.380
A whole virtual universe

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:43.160
(Depeche Mode) ♪ Let me take you on a train ♪

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:45.480
♪ Around the world and back ♪

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:48.200
People come to the Oasis for all the things they can do

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:52.080
♪ And you won't have to move, you just sit still ♪

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:55.940
But they stay because of all the things they can be.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:57.940
Art3mis: Can you feel this?

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:00.780
Parzival: Um... Yeah.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:03.800
It's the only place that feels like I mean anything.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.420
The Oasis was the brainchild of James Halliday.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:10.780
Hello. If you're watching this I'm dead.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:19.180
I created a hidden object, an Easter Egg. The first person to find the Egg will inherit half a trillion dollars.

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:23.400
And total control of the Oasis itself.

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:27.360
('Jump' by Van Halen plays)

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:31.880
Who is this "Parzival" and how the hell is he winning?

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:33.360
Find him.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.380
This isn't just a game!

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:42.620
I'm talking about actual life-and-death stuff. The Oasis, the world's most important economic resource.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.600
Sorrento: This is nothing less than a war for control of the future.

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:51.440
[Large, cascading explosion]

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:54.100
Welcome to the rebellion, Wade.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:56.100
♪ Might as well jump ♪

00:01:57.880 --> 00:01:59.880
♪ Go ahead and jump ♪

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:03.340
♪ Get in and jump ♪

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:06.420
Like many of you, I only came here to escape

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:12.180
But I found something much bigger than just myself.

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:14.180
Are you willing to fight?

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:17.400
Help us save the Oasis.

